Brief Summary: Interactive File Transfer with SFTP
SFTP allows you to securely transfer files between your local machine and a remote server through an interactive shell.

Key commands:

sftp user@host — Connect to a remote server
ls, cd — List and navigate remote files
lls, lcd — List and navigate local files
put filename — Upload a local file
get filename — Download a remote file
bye — Exit the SFTP session
SFTP is especially useful when you need to explore remote directories before transferring files.